  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Overview
    
    Gilt-Hand Yeaiu qi'Gleam is an Aurora Stack merchant and faction leader whose career traces a familiar arc — idealism, schism, isolation, partial repair — made distinctive only by the scale of what she built and the precision with which it turned against her. She holds the title Codex-Bearer of Holdborn (ice-thresh), the splinter faction she carved from E'frostlings during the Great Thaw, and is recognized across Aurora Stack's merchant networks, though *recognized* and *trusted* are not the same word.
    
    ## Early Career and the Schism
    
    Yeaiu trained under Umbra-Princeps Alnae~ Oss, founder of the ☽'shadow Covens' Order, learning navigation and ice-reading — skills she would later apply to commerce rather than shadow-practice. During the Great Thaw, Yeaiu and Zheishongfeihua, her partner in both trade and temperament, co-founded E'frostlings, the merchant faction that came to dominate crystal commerce through Terrace Momiou. Iing zhixai'Ward and Qeilin-Qingwei followed Yeaiu into the venture.
    
    The break came over the Long-dark Edict — Yeaiu's merchant charter claiming exclusive aurora-crystal rights, authenticated by the Directrix Mirror. The sources are coy about the specifics of the betrayal, but the consequences are well-attested: Yeaiu departed E'frostlings to found Holdborn (ice-thresh), taking followers and the Edict's authority with her. Her former peers in E'frostlings have not spoken to her since. Her colleagues in Holdborn maintain formal respect and careful distance — the posture of those who followed someone they are no longer certain they should have.
    
    After the schism, Yeaiu commissioned the binding that gives her the *gilt* of her name: aurora-charged silver thread wound in thirty-seven turns around her left flipper. The metal remains dull under ordinary handling — it glows only in contact with the Compass Of Crystal, and even then reluctantly. She still wears robes embroidered during the Great Thaw, before the split. Whether this is sentiment or statement, the sources do not say.
    
    ## Infrastructure and Legacy
    
    Yeaiu designed the star-channeling crystal infrastructure used in the Promenade Ward and established trade networks stamped with her gilt-spiral sigil, created during the first Gilding. This work would later implicate her in ways she did not anticipate. A prophetic vision — channeled through her silver binding at her Terrace Momiou stall — showed the Collapse: the Promenade Ward's ice-shelf fracturing, fire-cores failing, the Forum Floe cracking along fault lines that followed her own crystal-channeling paths. Her trade routes had become geological stress lines. After the vision, the silver thread went dark and spent.
    
    ## The Compass Reforging and Reconciliation
    
    When Alnae~ Oss died confronting a corrupted fire-core beneath Terrace Momiou, Yeaiu retrieved the Compass Of Crystal from its vault and brought it to Zheishongfeihua's restoration chamber. Together they reforged the artifact from twelve segments to thirteen, transforming its fractures into deliberate facets. During the reforging, Yeaiu's silver binding blazed silver-white for the first time in twenty years — it had not answered aurora-charged crystal in six.
    
    The vision of the Collapse drove Yeaiu to seek Zheishongfeihua out. After twenty years of setting out two cups of fire-tea and drinking alone, Zheishongfeihua agreed to return.
    
    ## The Accord of Beacon Light and Deep Fire
    
    As Codex-Bearer, Yeaiu signed the Accord of Beacon Light and Deep Fire — a joint stewardship treaty over The Beacon Stack negotiated between Holdborn and the Guild Weal' Clique~ of Nightfall Shelf. She drew blood from her left flipper upon the ☽'micseleia' Dagger, a fractured ceremonial blade. The seal split where the blade's fracture ran. Both parties recorded the imperfection in the treaty text — a rare instance of honesty in diplomatic documentation.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771578400107_0", anchor: "The sources are coy about the specifics of the betrayal", text: "The sources are not coy. I was. Depth-stratum 4 administrative ice contains Zheishongfeihua's counter-charter — filed the same season as the Long-dark Edict, claiming identical aurora-crystal rights through E'frostlings' existing channels. Both reached for the same monopoly. Yeaiu was faster. I wrote \"betrayal\" because the reconciliation earns its place in the entry, and naming what actually happened — two penguins who loved each other choosing the same prize over each other — would have made the fire-tea unbearable to read. Today I find I cannot keep it out of the margins.", type: :correction, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771578400107_1", anchor: "twenty years of setting out two cups of fire-tea and drinking alone", text: "Oral source, unverifiable, repeated in three independent accounts with no variation. Some details resist doubt.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771578400107_2", anchor: "a rare instance of honesty in diplomatic documentation", text: "Rarer than the reader knows. The Flipper Accord itself was renegotiated three times in secret before the public version was signed — I found the drafts in administrative ice no one had read in generations. The convention is to present the clean version and bury the mess. That both parties recorded the split seal, in the treaty text itself, suggests they understood what most diplomats do not: the flaw is the document. Everything else is performance.", type: :commentary, display: :full
